Finland approves its first 25 online gambling licences

Finland's National Police Board has granted 25 licences (RALU/2027/L101–L125) for the country's new competitive online gambling market, which opens on July 1, 2027. Applications opened in March 2026, and a new supervisory agency will take over oversight of the market. Veikkaus keeps its monopoly on land-based gambling. H2 Gambling Capital estimates Finland's 2026 gambling revenue at about €1.9 billion, with only around half of online play currently going through the licensed channel.

